Feature: Moving-Average & RSI Showcase
  Primary timeframe: 1d
  Parameter fast default 10
  Parameter slow default 30
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 5

  # Showcase demo (NOT profit-tuned): exercises the MA trend-filter primitives
  # not shown elsewhere — price-vs-SMA/EMA states and crosses, SMA-vs-EMA
  # crosses — plus rsi_crosses_50, the pivot STATE primitives, and stddev.

  Background:
    Given a series vol defined as stddev(20)

  Scenario: Enter long when the fast SMA crosses above the slow EMA in an uptrend
    Given no open position
    When sma_crosses_above_ema(fast, slow)
    And price_above_sma(fast)
    And vol is above 1
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Enter long when price reclaims the fast SMA above the daily pivot
    Given no open position
    When price_crosses_above_sma(fast)
    And price_above_pivot(P)
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long when the fast SMA crosses below the slow EMA
    Given a long position is open
    When sma_crosses_below_ema(fast, slow)
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Exit long when price breaks below the fast SMA
    Given a long position is open
    When price_crosses_below_sma(fast)
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short when price loses the slow EMA below the pivot
    Given no open position
    When price_crosses_below_ema(slow)
    And price_below_pivot(P)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Enter short on an RSI 50 breakdown below both averages
    Given no open position
    When rsi_crosses_50()
    And price_below_sma(slow)
    And price_below_ema(slow)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short when price reclaims the slow EMA
    Given a short position is open
    When price_crosses_above_ema(slow)
    Then short_exit

  Scenario: Exit short when price holds above the fast EMA
    Given a short position is open
    When price_above_ema(fast)
    Then short_exit
